A||||13||David DeVoe||Help!! Need ideas on broken bolt||||5||
Z||000000||David DeVoe||10-04-2001||04:09 PM||||Well, now I've done it. Drilled out a broken exaust bolt then broke the easy out off down in the hole. Cant get the easy out out, can't drill it with anything I've got. Any ideas at all????? God this head is in fine shape, hate to junk it because of a bolt. Im beginning to reasess my desire to own a Fiero.||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-04-2001||05:18 PM||||Is a head on a 2.8?  They are about as common as white bread - used in Fieros to Camaros.  I know it might not sound like it, but it might be easiest to just get a replacement H.O. head from a salvage yard.  Bring the head with, so you can verify the replacement has the big valves, etc., just like your original head.<P>2.8 heads can be had pretty cheap, and I imagine swapping the head is going to be less trouble overall than trying to get an easy-out out, while it's still in the car.<P>EDM-ing the bolt extractor out probably won't be cheap, and you'll have to pull the head off for that anyway.<P>If you swap heads, you can enjoy your car sooner, and mess with saving the old head later  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Probably not what you really wanted to hear.  But it's what Stu'd do! <BR>  ||||reg||5
Z||000002||David DeVoe||10-04-2001||05:46 PM||||Stu,<BR>Thanks for the input. The engine is in a zillion pieces in my garage the head is on the bench. I was just going to remove that dammn-- bolt and take the heads to the shop for a valve job. Oh well back to the drawing board.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||10-04-2001||06:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by David DeVoe:<BR><B>Stu,<BR>Thanks for the input. The engine is in a zillion pieces in my garage the head is on the bench. I was just going to remove that dammn-- bolt and take the heads to the shop for a valve job. Oh well back to the drawing board.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey David!<BR>If you were going to take it to a shop anyways, why not ask how much they charge to extract the bolt???<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||10-04-2001||09:23 PM||||i was thinking same thing wrecker. let them do it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||10-04-2001||09:44 PM||||I have been successful on getting these out.  Buy a high quality center punch. Cheap ones will be a waste of time. The tap is extremely hard high carbon steel and is very brittle.  What you have to do is break the tap into pieces.  Crack a piece off and work it out and repeat.  Teaching metal shop to high school kids using taps gave me a lot of practice. BTW Don't forget to use safety glasses because the pieces break with a lot of potential momentum.  Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||maryjane||10-04-2001||09:55 PM||||I work in a machine shop and have used Skitime's method sucessfully quite a few times. If you get it out, make sure you blow the hole out good and then you will probably have to run a tap in again. Use a NEW tap, good quality, not a dull one. Lots of oil and work it in a little at a time. There may be little bits of the broken tool still lodged in the hole and could cause the new tap to bind, so take it easy. Good luck.<P>Oops, It's an easy out, not a tap. Not nearly as easy to break apart. sorry.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||ka4nkf||10-04-2001||10:03 PM||||Skitime is right.<BR>I have got them out another way also. If you have a torch you can heat it up to cherry red and this will take the hardness out and then you can drill  good luck||||reg||1
Z||000008||David DeVoe||10-11-2001||12:27 AM||||Thanks for all the ideas guys. Lets see now.....the guy at the shop wanted 50 bucks to get it out. I can get another head for 40 so thats out.<BR>I heated it up real hot and whacked it with a punch and the darn thing cracked. I had a helluva time getting all the crap out but I did, ran a tap in it and all is well. Now I'll see what else I can screw up<BR>Dave||||reg||1
